  {
   "text": "Four Final Fantasy Commander decks were released together with Final Fantasy on June 13, 2025. These are meant to be on-ramps to Commander , with new cards and reprints.",
   "scene": 0,
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "While Commander precons are usually themed around certain characters, colors, or strategies, the twist with these is that each one is built around a single Final Fantasy game – specifically VI , VII , X , and XIV .",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "Each deck introduces 25 never-before-seen Commander cards to Magic: The Gathering . All reprints in the Commander decks have new art, suited to the Final Fantasy theme. The nonland reprints use art from within that deck’s game, while lands can appear from any of the four games included in the product. Secret Rendezvous appears in four different versions. The decks have a MSRP of $69.99.",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "Cards have the FIC expansion code. The face commanders and the secondary commanders are #1-8. The other new cards are #9-#100. Extended art Legendaries are #101-193. Borderless Sagas are #194-200 and the borderless commanders are #201-208. Surge foil commanders are #220-227 and their borderless variants are #209-216. Secret Rendezvous variants are #217-219. The Buy-a-Box promo is #220. The reprints (all with new art) are #229-441. Command Tower variants are #484-486. New cards with the FIC set code are permitted in the Commander, Legacy, and Vintage formats. Previously printed cards with the FIC set code are legal for play in any format where a card with the same name is permitted.",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "Card numbers FIC #442-465 are the cards in the Final Fantasy Holiday Release Scene Boxes . FIC #466-477 (and FIN #564-571) are \"track foil\" alternate art Chocobo Bundle cards by Japanese artists and illustrators. Many of these cards incorporate chocobos into their artwork. FIC 478-482 are the Chocobo track foil lands, FIC 483 is the Chocobo Bundle promo . FIC 484-486 are alternate art Command Towers . Note that FIC #469 is the only non- Final Fantasy Chocobo Bundle card: Snapcaster Mage .",
   "scene": 2,
   "section": "Additional FIC cards"
  },
  {
   "text": "Each package contains:",
   "scene": 3,
   "section": "Contents"
  },
  {
   "text": "1 ready-to-play 100-card Commander deck 1 traditional foil face commander 1 traditional foil featured commander 98 non-foil cards",
   "scene": 3,
   "section": "Contents"
  },
  {
   "text": "10 double-sided tokens Counter Blitz contains 4 punch-out counter cards and 6 double-sided tokens.",
   "scene": 3,
   "section": "Contents"
  },
  {
   "text": "1 Collector Booster Sample Pack (2 cards)",
   "scene": 3,
   "section": "Contents"
  },
  {
   "text": "All four of these decks were also available in a Collector's Edition, retailing for MSRP $149.99. Each deck featured all 100 of the cards in a special surge foil treatment.",
   "scene": 4,
   "section": "Collector's Edition"
  },
  {
   "text": "The four decks in their entirety were not made available on Magic: The Gathering Arena but the four face commanders and four back-up commanders were added for players to craft on release of the main set.",
   "scene": 5,
   "section": "Magic: The Gathering Arena"
  },
  {
   "text": "A Final Fantasy VI -based deck centered around self-mill and reviving creatures from the graveyard . Thematically this deck rebuilds its large ensemble of characters in the World of Ruin , its theming plays into that section of the story.",
   "scene": 7,
   "section": "Revival Trance"
  },
